    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1950-p3.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "In standard form the equation is \\(4x^2-8x+5=0.\\) By Vieta’s formulas, the sum of its roots is \\[ -\\frac{-8}{4}=2. \\] This value is not among choices A through D.\n\nThus, the correct answer is E.",
      "hints": [
        "Rewrite the equation in descending powers of \\(x\\)",
        "For \\(ax^2+bx+c=0,\\) the sum of the roots is \\(-\\frac{b}{a}\\)"
      ],
